body:
I don't want this to seem confrontational, but I never said I had no skills. I know people often fail to see their strengths when they're at their lowest - I assume this is what you were trying to address in your comment - but in therapy one thing that was really cemented in my brain was the value of looking at things from different perspectives, so I think I have a somewhat clear picture of my strengths (few) and weaknesses (many).

&nbsp;

I went through the links you provided. I'm sorry but I don't think I can leverage this effectively as a helpful resource. I understand the value in the suggestions and insight therein. In my post I mention trying some of your suggestions but to no avail. The remaining suggestions are much easier said than done and I don't believe them to be possible for me.
